From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0/2] nfc: nxp-nci: support an optional reference clock

Allow platforms with an external NCI reference clock to describe and use it.
Prepare the clock before raising controller enable and release it after cold
mode. Keep one vote across active transitions and preserve clockless boards.
Propagate lookup and enable errors before changing GPIO or software mode so a
failed open remains cold and can retry.

The PN547 on Madai uses a pin-controlled XO buffer. Board integration is kept
separate: the Madai board file is absent from this receiving tree. The removal
locking and receive-lifetime fixes are also maintained separately.

